# 🎨 Lash Bloom Studio Styleguide

## ✨ Brand Voice & Personality

**Premium • Elegant • Trustworthy • Feminine**

- **Tone**: Professional yet warm, confident but approachable
- **Language**: Clear, direct, no jargon. Use Latvian primarily, with Russian/English support
- **Approach**: Focus on transformation, self-care, and confidence
- **Avoid**: Aggressive sales language, technical beauty terminology, rushed communication

## 🎯 Typography Rules

### Font Hierarchy
- **Headlines**: Fraunces serif (`font-serif`) - Emotional, elegant, attention-grabbing
- **UI/Body**: Manrope sans (`font-sans`) - Clean, readable, functional
- **Never**: Mix serif in UI elements or sans in display headlines

### Size Scale
```css
H1: text-4xl md:text-5xl (hero sections)
H2: text-3xl md:text-4xl (page sections)  
H3: text-2xl md:text-3xl (subsections)
H4: text-xl md:text-2xl (component titles)
Body Large: text-xl (introductions)
Body: text-base (default reading)
Small: text-sm (captions, meta)
```

### Line Height
- **Headlines**: `leading-tight` (1.2x) for impact
- **Body**: `leading-relaxed` (1.625x) for readability
- **UI**: `leading-normal` (1.5x) for interface elements

## 🎨 Color Usage

### Primary Palette
```scss
--brand-bg: #FAF8F7 (porcelain)
--brand-text: #1C1A1A (ink)  
--brand-accent: #CFB27C (gold)
```

### Supporting Colors
```scss
--blush: #EEDDE2 (highlights, backgrounds)
--mauve: #D9C2C8 (borders, subtle accents)
```

### Usage Rules
- **Gold**: CTAs, active states, icons, hover effects
- **Ink**: Primary text, borders in high contrast
- **Porcelain**: Main backgrounds, card backgrounds
- **Blush**: Soft backgrounds, gentle highlights
- **Mauve**: Borders, subtle separators, disabled states

### ❌ Color Don'ts
- No blue gradients (conflicts with brand warmth)
- No hard-coded hex values in components
- No pure black (#000) or pure white (#FFF)
- No neon or saturated colors

## 📐 Spacing Rhythm

### Base Scale: 8px Unit System
```scss
xs: 4px   (0.5 unit)
sm: 8px   (1 unit)  
md: 16px  (2 units)
lg: 24px  (3 units) ⭐ Primary
xl: 32px  (4 units) ⭐ Primary  
2xl: 40px (5 units) ⭐ Primary
```

### Section Spacing
- **Tight**: `py-8 md:py-12` (32px/48px)
- **Normal**: `py-12 md:py-16` (48px/64px)
- **Generous**: `py-16 md:py-20` (64px/80px) ⭐ Preferred
- **Hero**: `py-20 md:py-24` (80px/96px)
- **Extra**: `py-24 md:py-32` (96px/128px)

### Component Spacing
- **Cards**: `p-6` or `p-8` internal padding
- **Buttons**: `px-8 py-6` for large, `px-6 py-3` for default
- **Form fields**: `mb-6` between fields
- **Grid gaps**: `gap-6` or `gap-8` standard

## 🎭 Motion Guidelines

### Animation Timing
- **Content entrance**: 240ms (0.24s)
- **Stagger delay**: 60ms (0.06s)
- **Hover effects**: 200ms (0.2s)
- **Micro-interactions**: 150ms (0.15s)

### Easing
- **Content**: `ease-out` for natural feeling
- **Hover**: `ease` for responsiveness
- **Complex**: `cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1)`

### Animation Patterns
```javascript
// Entry Animation
fadeInUp: {
  initial: { opacity: 0, y: 20 },
  animate: { opacity: 1, y: 0 },
  transition: { duration: 0.24, ease: "easeOut" }
}

// Hover Scale
whileHover: { scale: 1.02 }
transition: { duration: 0.2 }

// Stagger Container
staggerChildren: 0.06
```

### Motion Rules
- ✅ Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`
- ✅ Use for feedback and delight
- ❌ Never animate purely for decoration
- ❌ No animations over 500ms without user control

## ♿ Accessibility Checklist

### Color & Contrast
- [ ] 4.5:1 contrast for normal text
- [ ] 3:1 contrast for large text (18pt+)
- [ ] Never rely on color alone for meaning
- [ ] Test with color blindness simulators

### Typography
- [ ] Minimum 16px base font size
- [ ] Maximum line length 75 characters
- [ ] Sufficient line spacing (1.5x minimum)
- [ ] Clear heading hierarchy (H1→H6)

### Interaction
- [ ] All interactive elements keyboard accessible
- [ ] Focus indicators visible and clear
- [ ] Touch targets minimum 44px
- [ ] ARIA labels on icon buttons

### Structure
- [ ] Semantic HTML elements (`<main>`, `<section>`, `<article>`)
- [ ] Proper heading structure (no skipped levels)
- [ ] Alt text for all images
- [ ] Form labels properly associated

## 📸 Imagery Guidance

### Photography Style
- **Mood**: Soft, natural lighting with warm tones
- **Composition**: Clean, uncluttered, focus on eyes/lashes
- **Color grading**: Warm highlights, avoid cool blues
- **Models**: Diverse representation, authentic expressions

### Technical Requirements
- **Format**: WebP with JPEG fallback
- **Optimization**: Next.js Image component always
- **Responsive**: Multiple sizes for different viewports
- **Lazy loading**: Default behavior for performance

### Placeholder Strategy
- **Development**: Use `bg-grain bg-porcelain` for image placeholders
- **Loading**: Skeleton components while images load
- **Fallback**: Graceful degradation if images fail

## ✅ Design Do's & Don'ts

### ✅ DO
- Use serif fonts for emotional headlines
- Maintain generous whitespace for luxury feel
- Keep interactions subtle and refined
- Use gold sparingly for maximum impact
- Design mobile-first, enhance for desktop
- Test with real content, not Lorem Ipsum
- Follow 8px spacing grid consistently
- Use shadcn/ui components as foundation

### ❌ DON'T
- Mix serif and sans inappropriately
- Use harsh drop shadows or heavy borders
- Overcrowd interfaces with too many elements
- Use animations longer than 300ms for UI
- Create custom components when shadcn exists
- Use blue colors (conflicts with brand)
- Hard-code colors or spacing values
- Ignore mobile experience

## 🎯 Brand Application

### Logo Usage
- Minimum clear space: 2x the height of the text
- Never stretch, skew, or alter proportions
- Use on high contrast backgrounds only
- Maintain readability at all sizes

### Voice Applications
- **Headers**: Confident, clear benefit statements
- **CTAs**: Action-oriented, urgency without pressure  
- **Descriptions**: Features + benefits, focus on transformation
- **Forms**: Clear instructions, encouraging tone

